# Fataplus Database Guidelines

## 🗃️ General

- Use NuxtHub's `database/` directory for schema definitions.
- Each table should be defined in its own `.ts` file.
- Use clear, lowercase, snake_case naming for tables and fields.
- Avoid storing derived or computed data — calculate on read when needed.
- Use default timestamps (`created_at`, `updated_at`) when useful.

## 📦 Core Tables

### `products.ts`

- `name`: string — product name (e.g. "Tomates")
- `price`: number — price per unit (e.g. per kg)
- `unit`: string — "kg", "l", etc.
- `stock`: number — current stock available
- `image`: string (blob ref) — product image URL or ID

### `orders.ts`

- `user_id`: reference to `users.id`
- `product_id`: reference to `products.id`
- `quantity`: number
- `total`: number (calculated at checkout)
- `status`: enum ("pending", "confirmed", "delivered")

### `users.ts`

- `name`, `email`, `password`
- `role`: enum ("farmer", "buyer", "trainer", "admin")

## 🎓 LMS Tables

### `courses.ts`

- `title`, `description`, `cover`, `instructor`

### `lessons.ts`

- `course_id`: reference to `courses.id`
- `title`, `content`, `video`

### `progress.ts`

- `user_id`, `course_id`, `lesson_id`
- `completed`: boolean or timestamp

## 🧠 AI Assistant

### `messages.ts`

- `user_id`: reference to `users.id`
- `content`: string
- `type`: enum ("user", "ai")
- `timestamp`: datetime

## ✅ Notes

- Add `vectorize/` entries for content used in AI assistant (like lessons).
- Use `blob/` for course media, product images.
- Use clear field types to help Copilot and Cline generate forms and queries faster.